  "term": "hyperalgesia",
  "definition": "Hyperalgesia is an unusually heightened pain response in which even mildly harmful stimulation causes more pain or discomfort than expected. It can result from damage to soft tissue with pain-sensing nerve endings or from injury to a peripheral nerve.",
